{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["# Feature Engineering Notebook for Refinery Predictive Maintenance\n",
              "\n",
              "This notebook demonstrates how to transform raw sensor streams (stored as Parquet) into a feature matrix suitable for training a predictive‑maintenance model. The steps include:\n",
              "* Loading raw sensor data\n",
              "* Resampling and aligning timestamps\n",
              "* Computing sliding‑window statistical features (mean, std, min, max, kurtosis)\n",
              "* Extracting frequency‑domain features via FFT\n",
              "* Creating a binary failure label (7‑day horizon) from maintenance logs\n",
              "* Saving the engineered dataset for downstream model training.\n",
              "\n",
              "The notebook is written for a **refinery‑focused** environment – the tag list matches the collector script. Adjust the `RAW_DATA_PATH` and `MAINTENANCE_LOG_PATH` variables to point to your actual data locations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["import os\n",
              "import pandas as pd\n",
              "import numpy as np\n",
              "from pathlib import Path\n",
              "\n",
              "# ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
              "# Configuration – adjust to your environment\n              "# ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
              "RAW_DATA_PATH = Path('..', 'data', 'raw', 'sensors')   # Parquet file with raw OPC-UA streams\n",
              "MAINTENANCE_LOG_PATH = Path('..', 'data', 'raw', 'maintenance_logs', 'work_orders.parquet')\n",
              "FEATURE_OUTPUT_PATH = Path('..', 'data', 'processed', 'features.parquet')\n",
              "LABEL_OUTPUT_PATH = Path('..', 'data', 'processed', 'failure_label.parquet')\n",
              "\n",
              "# Ensure output directory exists\n",
              "FEATURE_OUTPUT_PATH.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 1️⃣ Load raw sensor data\n",
              "\n",
              "The collector writes a Parquet file with a column per OPC‑UA tag and a UTC timestamp index.\n",
              "We load it into a DataFrame and set the timestamp as the index."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["# Load the most recent Parquet file (you may have many; here we pick the latest)\n",
              "parquet_files = sorted(RAW_DATA_PATH.glob('*.parquet'))\n",
              "if not parquet_files:\n",
              "    raise FileNotFoundError(f'No parquet files found in {RAW_DATA_PATH}')\n",
              "raw_df = pd.read_parquet(parquet_files[-1])\n",
              "\n",
              "# Ensure timestamp column exists – the collector writes `timestamp` in ISO‑format\n",
              "if 'timestamp' in raw_df.columns:\n",
              "    raw_df['timestamp'] = pd.to_datetime(raw_df['timestamp'], utc=True)\n",
              "    raw_df = raw_df.set_index('timestamp')\n",
              "else:\n",
              "    raw_df.index = pd.to_datetime(raw_df.index, utc=True)\n",
              "\n",
              "# Sort by time just in case\n",
              "raw_df = raw_df.sort_index()\n",
              "raw_df.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 2️⃣ Resample to a uniform cadence\n",
              "\n",
              "Refinery sensors may emit at slightly irregular intervals. We resample to **1 Hz** (once per second) using forward‑fill for missing values."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["resampled_df = raw_df.resample('1S').ffill()\n",
              "# Keep a reasonable window – drop the first 5 minutes to avoid start‑up artifacts\n",
              "resampled_df = resampled_df.iloc[5*60:]\n",
              "resampled_df.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 3️⃣ Sliding‑window statistical features\n",
              "\n",
              "For each tag we compute: mean, std, min, max, skew, kurtosis over a **30‑second** window, stepping every 10 seconds. These capture short‑term dynamics useful for RNN models."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["WINDOW = '30S'   # 30‑second window\n",
              "STEP = '10S'     # slide every 10 seconds\n",
              "\n",
              "def rolling_stats(df: pd.DataFrame):\n",
              "    feats = []\n",
              "    for col in df.columns:\n",
              "        series = df[col]\n",
              "        # basic stats\n",
              "        feats.append(series.rolling(WINDOW).mean().rename(f'{col}_mean'))\n",
              "        feats.append(series.rolling(WINDOW).std().rename(f'{col}_std'))\n",
              "        feats.append(series.rolling(WINDOW).min().rename(f'{col}_min'))\n",
              "        feats.append(series.rolling(WINDOW).max().rename(f'{col}_max'))\n",
              "        # higher‑order moments\n",
              "        feats.append(series.rolling(WINDOW).skew().rename(f'{col}_skew'))\n",
              "        feats.append(series.rolling(WINDOW).kurt().rename(f'{col}_kurt'))\n",
              "    return pd.concat(feats, axis=1)\n",
              "\n",
              "stat_df = rolling_stats(resampled_df)\n",
              "# Down‑sample to the step frequency (10 s) to reduce data size\n",
              "stat_df = stat_df.resample(STEP).last().dropna()\n",
              "stat_df.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 4️⃣ Frequency‑domain features (FFT magnitude)\n",
              "\n",
              "We compute the magnitude of the first few FFT bins (up to 0.5 Hz) for each tag within the same sliding window. This captures periodic vibrations or oscillations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["def fft_features(df: pd.DataFrame, n_bins: int = 5):\n",
              "    feats = []\n",
              "    for col in df.columns:\n",
              "        # Apply FFT on each window; use pandas rolling with a custom lambda\n",
              "        def window_fft(window):\n",
              "            # pad/trim to nearest power of two for speed\n",
              "            arr = np.asarray(window)\n",
              "            # Compute real FFT\n",
              "            fft_vals = np.abs(np.fft.rfft(arr))\n",
              "            # Return first n_bins magnitudes (skip the DC component)\n",
              "            return fft_vals[1:n_bins+1]\n",
              "        # Apply rolling and expand resulting array into separate columns\n",
              "        fft_series = df[col].rolling(WINDOW).apply(window_fft, raw=False)\n",
              "        # fft_series is a series of ndarrays – explode into columns\n",
              "        for i in range(n_bins):\n",
              "            feats.append(fft_series.apply(lambda x: x[i] if isinstance(x, np.ndarray) else np.nan)\n",
              "                         .rename(f'{col}_fft_bin{i+1}'))\n",
              "    return pd.concat(feats, axis=1)\n",
              "\n",
              "fft_df = fft_features(resampled_df)\n",
              "fft_df = fft_df.resample(STEP).last().dropna()\n",
              "fft_df.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 5️⃣ Combine statistical and frequency features\n",
              "\n",
              "We concatenate the two feature sets, drop any rows with NaNs (edges of the windows), and end up with a tidy matrix ready for model training."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["features_df = pd.concat([stat_df, fft_df], axis=1).dropna()\n",
              "features_df.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 6️⃣ Create binary failure label (7‑day horizon)\n",
              "\n",
              "We assume the maintenance logs contain a column `equipment_id` and a timestamp `failure_time`. For each timestamp in the feature matrix we assign `1` if a failure of the same equipment occurs within the next 7 days, otherwise `0`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["# Load maintenance logs – expects columns: equipment_id, failure_time (UTC)\n",
              "maint_df = pd.read_parquet(MAINTENANCE_LOG_PATH)\n",
              "maint_df['failure_time'] = pd.to_datetime(maint_df['failure_time'], utc=True)\n",
              "\n",
              "# For simplicity we treat all tags as belonging to the same "equipment"; in a real project you would map tags to equipment IDs.\n",
              "LABEL_HORIZON_DAYS = 7\n",
              "label_series = []\n",
              "for ts in features_df.index:\n",
              "    horizon_end = ts + pd.Timedelta(days=LABEL_HORIZON_DAYS)\n",
              "    # any failure within the window?\n",
              "    has_failure = maint_df[(maint_df['failure_time'] > ts) & (maint_df['failure_time'] <= horizon_end)].shape[0] > 0\n",
              "    label_series.append(1 if has_failure else 0)\n",
              "\n",
              "label_df = pd.DataFrame({'failure_label': label_series}, index=features_df.index)\n",
              "label_df.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 7️⃣ Persist engineered features and label\n",
              "\n",
              "We store the feature matrix and the label side‑by‑side as separate Parquet files for downstream model training."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["features_df.to_parquet(FEATURE_OUTPUT_PATH)\n",
              "label_df.to_parquet(LABEL_OUTPUT_PATH)\n",
              "print(f'Features saved to {FEATURE_OUTPUT_PATH}')\n",
              "print(f'Label saved to {LABEL_OUTPUT_PATH}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["### 🎉 Finished!\n",
              "You now have a clean, time‑indexed feature set (`features.parquet`) and a binary failure label (`failure_label.parquet`). The next step is to feed these into the model training notebook (e.g., `02_model_training.ipynb`)."
   ]
  }
